&gt; Maps route deeper into books and answers</div><aside class="card redline"><h2>Risk Boundary</h2><p>Adverse-event reports, compensation, settlements, proven causation, and official statistics are different categories and must not be merged.</p></aside></section><section class="section wrap"><h2>Relationship Lines</h2><p class="lead">These are defined lines, not red-string insinuations.</p><div class="grid"><article class="card redline"><span class="label">Causation warning · Confirmed Record</span><h3>Adverse Event Report → Causation Claim</h3><p>A report is a signal, not proof of causation by itself.</p></article><article class="card redline"><span class="label">Compensation record · Confirmed Record</span><h3>Compensation Program → Financial Records</h3><p>Compensated claims must be separated from pending claims and reported events.</p></article><article class="card redline"><span class="label">Human cost · Confirmed Record</span><h3>Medical Policy → Human Cost</h3><p>Public-health claims require dated datasets and clear categories.</p></article></div></section><section class="section wrap"><h2>Connected Power Atlas Nodes</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card redline"><span class="label">Power Atlas · Confirmed Record</span><h3>Medical Power</h3><p>A policy and compensation node for medical institutions, adverse-event reporting boundaries, vaccine compensation, pharma damages, public-health power, and evidence discipline.</p><a class="btn" href="atlas-medical-power.html">Open Node</a></article><article class="card redline"><span class="label">Power Atlas · Confirmed Record</span><h3>Black File</h3><p>The Black File is the gateway map that routes readers through intelligence, crime networks, contractors, secret societies, war, surveillance, psychology, human cost, and symbolic systems.</p><a class="btn" href="atlas-black-file.html">Open Node</a></article></div><h2>Connected Evidence Vault Lanes</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><span class="label